 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -19 & 15\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186342121 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ba6ce214-f348-57ed-8c0e-e75dd14f4628" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342121 #edb/ref 1074 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -12 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -19 & 15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -19 & 15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y-5z &=6 \\\\ 0x+y+3z &=-4 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-9,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186363080 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363080 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131498" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363080 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363080 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186363080 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a7ba9088-1a5a-5dc8-89fa-4feea7488ee8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363080 #edb/ref 1074 "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+5y+0z &=3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n-x+5y=3\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=5y-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5y-3 \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$, $z$ (free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5y-3 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186363081 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363081 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363081 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363081 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363081 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363081 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363081 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363081 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186363082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363081 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "59f088e4-8267-5e3a-8395-4af841304036" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363082 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [1759218636308